      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-20T16:32:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This makes sense to me now:\n\n```\n- sys_clock_hw_cycles_per_sec(): This function returns the number of hardware clock cycles in one second.\n\n- USEC_PER_SEC: This constant represents the number of microseconds in one second (1,000,000).\n\n- USEC_PER_SEC / sys_clock_hw_cycles_per_sec(): This calculation gives the duration of a single hardware clock cycle in microseconds, which essentially represents the resolution of a \"tick\" when converted to microseconds.\n\n- 2 * (single_tick_duration_in_usec): Since the comment states the maximum error threshold is \"two ticks,\" we multiply the duration of a single tick (in microseconds) by 2.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ae1fb028_2f889206",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 54
      },
